===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|pre|historic|t1=[[before]]}}, ''q.v.'', similar to slightly earlier {{m|en|ante-historic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɒɹɪk|s=4}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|properly}} Of or relating to the [[epoch]] before written [[record]].
#* '''1832''' October, ''Foreign Quarterly Review'', p. 369:
#*: Was it then in a '''pre-historic''' time that the Romans wandered into these lands?
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1981|author=William Irwin Thompson|authorlink=William Irwin Thompson|title=The Time Falling Bodies Take to Light: Mythology, Sexuality and the Origins of Culture|publisher=Rider/Hutchinson & Co.|location=London|page=137|passage=The cartoon image of '''prehistoric''' woman being dragged by the hair by her caveman-husband probably conditions the perceptions of archaeologists far more than they realize.}}
# {{lb|en|inexact|_|or|_|jocular}} [[ancient|Ancient]]; [[very]] [[old]], [[outdated]], etc.

